  "account": {
   "agency": "Department of Health and Human Services",
   "bureau": "General Provisions",
   "canonical_account_id": "ACC-HHS-GP-MEDICARE-LIMITATION",
   "canonical_name": "Limitation for Title XVIII of the Social Security Act",
   "display_order": 24,
   "fund_type": "general",
   "historical_identifiers": null,
   "historical_names": null,
   "notes": "A general-provision line printed only for FY2026 Enacted (the JES and H.Rept. 119-696 p.392, 2,000; '---' in the FY2027 columns). The provision of P.L. 119-75 it reflects is not identified here -- the Title II general provisions carry no section naming title XVIII with that figure; to be confirmed. Vision read H.Rept. 119-696's label as 'mitation ...' (the page image prints 'Limitation ...'). The FY2026 line is P.L. 119-75 Division B sec. 241 (PDF p.120, 140 Stat. 293): CMS shall not apply the distance requirements of SSA sec. 1820(c)(2)(B)(i)(I) to certain critical access hospitals -- a title XVIII provision the FY2026 explanatory statement lists as 'a new provision related to title XVIII of the Social Security Act' (p.245) and its table scores at 2,000 (p.296). Not in the FY2021 or FY2022 bills, Budget Appendix language or laws (searched for '1820(c)(2)(B)' and 'distance requirement'). Its confirmed absences, which rested on tables' silence, were retired 2026-10-08 (owner).",
